invariant: INV-66
file: src/widemul_p256.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh p256-adx
reason: widemul_p256_adx answers yes under CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX alone, so a
  session whose caller states nothing about the multiply runs MULX's
  products on its private scalar, whose timing that caller has not stated.
  Every byte stays right. bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into
  the copy under CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX alone, and the qemu lane runs it for
  x86-64.

